@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@productA = 11111111-1111-1111-1111-111111111111
@productB = 22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222
@productC = 33333333-3333-3333-3333-333333333333

### Health
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### List products and inventory
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/products

### Create and reserve an order
# @name createOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-Correlation-ID: assessment-run-001

{
  "customerReference": "customer-1001",
  "items": [
    {"productId": "{{productA}}", "quantity": 2},
    {"productId": "{{productB}}", "quantity": 1},
    {"productId": "{{productC}}", "quantity": 5}
  ]
}

### Pay successfully (IntelliJ resolves createOrder response variables)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.orderId}}/payments
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: assessment-payment-success-001

{
  "outcome": "SUCCESS"
}

### Cancel an order (replace the ID when not using response variables)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/orders/{{createOrder.response.body.orderId}}/cancellations
